I was unclear :)
It only costs a turn because I use a unique message to help identify
Teleportation.  Writing Elbereth takes a turn, wiping and rewriting my
message uses one other.  Instead, I do the following:
Turn 1: Write my unique message.
Turn 2: Attempt to write with a wand.  If it is Lightening, Fire, or
Digging, it identifies itself and I write Elbereth.  Otherwise, I
erase and rewrite my message using the wand, in the hopes that I'll
identify Speed Monster, Slow Monster, etc.

This is as opposed to:
Turn 1: Write my unique message.
Turn 2: Attempt to write with a wand, writing Elbereth regardless of
what the wand is.
Turn 3: Wipe Elbereth and write my unique message.

Of course, this is only useful when doing a mass wand ID session--if
you are only trying to identify a single wand, it makes no difference.


